{"schema_version": "1.0", "session_id": "70b335e0-3d97-4f29-a1d9-e63d642ceaf3", "team_id": "contest2026_062_PharosTech", "github_login": "yunline", "tool": "copilot", "seq": 5, "ts": "2026-08-12T17:19:11.310000+00:00", "role": "assistant", "text": "The documentation has been added cleanly. The README now covers the Makefile-mode additions without mentioning st77916.\n\nLet me verify there are no errors in the file (it's markdown, so no compile errors expected, but I'll confirm nothing broke).\n\nThe README now includes a complete description of what Makefile mode needs, following the st77916 Makefile as a blueprint:\n\n1. **`Make.defs` role** — registers the directory via `CONFIGURED_APPS +=`, with the `ifneq ($(CONFIG_...),)` guard, explaining the automatic `wildcard */Make.defs` collection chain.\n2. **`Makefile` role** — the two `include` statements explained:\n   - `include $(APPDIR)/Make.defs` (at top): pulls in apps global build definitions, `$(APPDIR)`, `INCDIR_PREFIX`, default CFLAGS, and the shared `include/` path exposure.\n   - `include $(APPDIR)/Application.mk` (at bottom): pulls in the generic build script that consumes `CSRCS` to generate compile/link rules, and must come after the source variable declarations.\n3. **The relationship** between the two — both are needed, each guarded by the driver's enable option, and neither one alone is sufficient.\n\nThe doc stays generic (uses `<driver_name>` and `CONFIG_<该驱动的使能配置项>`) with no mention of the st77916 driver."}
